# shell: desktop
# prefs: factory
# PDF Pane, the SDK's example of the kit's PDF view in a program's own
# window, from the Demos menu: blank until a document is chosen in the
# shell's panel, then its pages drawn by the view's workers in the
# example's own process, and the view's words in its status line.
wait 20
click 980 40
wait 4
menu-pick Demos
wait 4
expect-menu PDF Pane
menu-pick PDF Pane
wait 30
expect-title PDF Pane
note nothing open: the window says nothing at all
shot /tmp/trk_pdfpane_empty.png
key o ctrl
wait 30
expect-title Open
key Down
wait 4
key Return
wait 40
expect-no-title Open
expect-title PDF Pane - guide.pdf
expect-narrate 3 pages, with an outline.
expect-narrate Page 1 of 3
shot /tmp/trk_pdfpane_open.png
note the view takes the keys the program hands it
key End
wait 10
expect-narrate Page 3 of 3
key w ctrl
wait 10
expect-no-title PDF Pane
